{"title":"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems\">2002 AMC 12B #12</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems\">2002 AMC 10B #16</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For how many integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/3/a739c279dd5e08ea3d01c168e1a960497660a058.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac n{20-n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"57\" height=\"36\" /> the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perfect_square\" title=\"Perfect square\">square</a> of an integer?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a8fba0bf16c9a6d70ea6e6367598a4861e720e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 1 \\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 2 \\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 3 \\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 4 \\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/8/e38192f76f1acbfb0fde45c065c064f48107aed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 = \\frac{n}{20-n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"95\" height=\"33\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/f/dff5a847457c4beaa2c6809fc9d7b26ebcaa398e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> (note that the solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/a/36a68e8aa6ec6f48231ad80a4851f84bacf641b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> do not give any additional solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />). Then rewriting, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/9/629c3d6c6014672be5af1f5ce2c0d64107c402ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\frac{20x^2}{x^2 + 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"86\" height=\"40\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/8/438b58f52f15d4129d0e6432963a59c2540321bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{gcd}(x^2, x^2 + 1) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"19\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/4/664ca690c157c78ee252a0a45144c403a673dbcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Listing the factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aee8b3a293ae992f50be22981ede64c2a45c4f0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0, 1, 2 , 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"17\" /> are the only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/6/67632ae2dd0da8ca9cb44c6a185838c7b7167156.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"29\" /> solutions (respectively yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/6/956f55243dfad96ba735f2a22d68b2d98d814155.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 0, 10, 16, 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"122\" height=\"16\" />).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/8/79813fe3de65c5970b8c1b6eecc359c0042447ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/0/90037592859847a0d4c684f62aca389c1919c223.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;20$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> the fraction is negative, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/731fff2fc30062dd7135caff108b191df21ea8bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=20$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> it is not defined, and for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/17464b8d6f6b51eb6f087a9b1b8b31d8a2327143.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in\\{1,\\dots,9\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" /> it is between 0 and 1.\n</p><p>Thus we only need to examine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/02349576cee613512cdf301a365f06c0760acab5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/6/0b6c20ee88145b100d6de0337ce2c9c0155687f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in\\{10,\\dots,19\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/02349576cee613512cdf301a365f06c0760acab5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc1b21210db29332b1a7d9ce088fd457f23aeee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> we obviously get the squares <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>For prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> the fraction will not be an integer, as the denominator will not contain the prime in the numerator.\n</p><p>This leaves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/5/1c5465530c63878e98ea21ec9f383e5db084f1a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in\\{12,14,15,16,18\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"173\" height=\"18\" />, and a quick substitution shows that out of these only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c874a6ca8456dd226bf716c2edfdd97d1bfd7665.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/c/9dce59f6afb62825f31819ae31874cca35417bbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> yield a square. Therefore, there are only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/6/67632ae2dd0da8ca9cb44c6a185838c7b7167156.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"29\" /> solutions (respectively yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/6/956f55243dfad96ba735f2a22d68b2d98d814155.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 0, 10, 16, 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"122\" height=\"16\" />).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/5/b0512c8eefc61dacd8a2da37c7def70714e5bbfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{20-n} = k^2 \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"130\" height=\"33\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/c/e2c7d62172af0e738dd12f47f3f8ad8ef70cd65f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/e/1ce4098cee7c08b46beee35f922a528630ec6aba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20-n &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"84\" height=\"13\" />, otherwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/8/158c83df7af85c5e5065a53e368e68c7170fe952.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{20-n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"53\" height=\"33\" /> will be negative. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/7/bb779977e90809847bd0695738a271f9f4148b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le n \\le 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/e/9feb430d115aea0e9e86b02cdd2ae225b49642b5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0 = \\frac{0}{20-(0)} \\le \\frac{n}{20-n} \\le \\frac{19}{20-(19)} = 19\\]\" width=\"322\" height=\"42\" /> Checking all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/c/97c2596d89fcd8895256c85fdf94eb20d2034c98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le k^2 \\le 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as the possibilities. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/e/8de641a309fc5878c26baf699f2382b7d4b02b5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"29\" />\n</p><p>~ Nafer\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For all integers x, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is always a positive integer. So solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/7/85706c3e74ffcafd9f7149a8ae315fbebc829bd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{20-n} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"90\" height=\"36\" />, getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/02349576cee613512cdf301a365f06c0760acab5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/7/2573a65d987603a0e3b347d67704111a3bcd4849.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{20-n} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"90\" height=\"36\" />, getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee983588b47152fbc1486daa6749fdbe613e861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n =10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />. For all values n less than 0 and greater than 20, the value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/8/158c83df7af85c5e5065a53e368e68c7170fe952.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{20-n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"53\" height=\"33\" /> is negative, so now try values of n between 10 and 20. Quick substitution finds <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> which yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/2/b022dc8ef6d33931fc1ae3d27df3ea0a81b52936.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. 4 values, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/e/8de641a309fc5878c26baf699f2382b7d4b02b5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"29\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Simon's Favourite Factoring Trick.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/8/158c83df7af85c5e5065a53e368e68c7170fe952.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{20-n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"53\" height=\"33\" /> is an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, we multiply both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/5/2f579c5b39f26cd628e016aa0c0be2987a774991.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20-n$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" />. This gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12fd25e94d62b3cac4d613956f0a02293baca406.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=20k^2-nk^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" />. We subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/9/129f7740dad11b95146a15fbb522b1d4d7c66e35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" /> on both sides, then add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/4/484878972d61505600c4e5b5427f70922f7b4883.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$nk^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"17\" /> on both sides as a prerequisite for using Simon's Favorite Factoring Trick. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac4166d30d1264d2c5086cfc9ef57de83b40542e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k^2+1)(n-20)=20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"21\" />. We then consider the different factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/6/1e6b3b40399c6938049ecb3cc04ac54d1adc8579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> can be. It could be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/0/63058845d757d7167d0b5f1d2ed9329efae3c208.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2,4,5,10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. After checking case by case, we then are able to identify that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> values that also yield an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> value, meaning that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> values, so the correct answer is  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/e/8de641a309fc5878c26baf699f2382b7d4b02b5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"29\" />\n~CharmaineMa0729201\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to previous solutions, we can bound <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Then, we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/7/fd7c1a5f2dde10b900bf8d018f1159d1f11deb55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{20-n} = k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"99\" height=\"36\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Multiplying out the fraction and factoring, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad2127806a9adc9407183089654395882876bc62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(k^2 + 1) = k^2 \\cdot 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"21\" />. As before, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/2/ea270c7b2fe2a87b7ea2bf1fe93c63f7aaa65392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{gcd}(k^2 + 1, k^2) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"21\" />, so we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/0/100f4de862eecf5b31acec379eec4583c7be9f62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2 | n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"35\" height=\"21\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/b/17be3fe649808a4ff48bfdc0590f69ab99c79663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq k^2 \\leq 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"19\" />, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/5/0e5c83cc0c639fc2ed843bbe2d3d209fb478b104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> now has to be at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, so trying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/2/dd255c1b9e37fc67754d5e5de3c42dc3053b7bb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2 = 0, 1, 4, 9, 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" />, we get four possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/e/8de641a309fc5878c26baf699f2382b7d4b02b5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p><p>~LQS\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B\">2002 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Proble